---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TopNav from '../components/TopNav.astro';

const testAuditAsOf = '2026-04-27';
---

<Base
  title="Projects — Sebastian Rogala"
  description="Multi-tenant Education SaaS in production, Pipeforge (Claude Code orchestration), ProfitOfExile, and open-source contributions."
>
  <TopNav current="projects" />

  <main class="frame">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">Projects</div>
      <h1>Projects</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Two products in active development plus side projects and open-source contributions.
        The Pipeforge walkthrough and a knowledge-base sample sit underneath as deeper reads.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content">
      <h2>Products</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">Education SaaS</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Multi-tenant platform, launch customer in production.</p>
          <p>
            Course management and lead-operations across education tenants; ready for expansion
            onto additional customers. Stack: PHP 8.4 / Symfony 7.4 LTS / Doctrine 3 /
            PostgreSQL 16 / Redis 7 backend; Twig + Stimulus + Turbo + Tailwind front-end;
            Vitest + PHPUnit + Playwright on tests. Hexagonal modular monolith with full CQRS
            at the UseCase layer, async events via Symfony Messenger, 7 business modules.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="#how-quality-gets-enforced">enforcement details ↓</a>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">Pipeforge</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Personal Claude Code orchestration plugin and PostgreSQL MCP backend.</p>
          <p>
            Pipeline orchestration with templated commands, agent dispatch, skill-based prompts,
            and an MCP-backed tool layer over a PostgreSQL state store — plus a curated knowledge
            base of decisions about Pipeforge itself. Built from a personal need to coordinate
            work across multiple machines and parallel worktrees; not a product, the infrastructure
            I use daily.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="/projects/pipeforge">walkthrough →</a>
            <span class="sep">·</span>
            <a href="/projects/kb">knowledge base →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="audit-figure">
        <a
          href="/screenshots/07-test-audit-all-suites-clean.png"
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src="/screenshots/07-test-audit-all-suites-clean.png"
            alt="Test audit on the production Education SaaS: 4,190 PHP tests + 157 E2E, all clean, runtime 7m 13s"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>
          Test audit on the production Education SaaS (as of {testAuditAsOf}): 4,190 PHP tests +
          157 E2E green, 259 structured learnings logged in 7m 13s. Suites: PHPStan clean ·
          Unit 2674/2674 (8539 assertions) · Integration 459/459 · Functional 699/699 ·
          Smoke 201/201 · E2E 157/157.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 id="how-quality-gets-enforced">How quality gets enforced</h2>
      <p>
        The Education SaaS runs four independent custom enforcement layers in CI — every PR has
        to pass all four before it can merge.
      </p>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li>
          <strong>PHPStan 2 at level 8</strong> — plus 13 project-specific custom rules:
          entity-ID safety, tenant query safety (blocks direct <code>EntityManager</code> /
          <code>Connection</code> access outside repositories), and ADR-shape rules for the
          Action / UseCase / QueryAdapter / Port catalog. The CQRS seam is enforced at this
          layer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>PHPMD</strong> — hexagonal-tuned ruleset for code smells; complements PHPStan
          on style and maintainability fronts that static analysis doesn't cover.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deptrac</strong> — enforces 3 hexagonal layers
          (Domain → Application → Infrastructure) across 7 business modules. Vendor imports
          gated by layer; exceptions baselined and documented.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Custom Twig/Tailwind lint script</strong> — 6 project rules expressing UI
          conventions that off-the-shelf linters can't: component-only
          <code>&lt;twig:Button&gt;</code> (no raw <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> in pages),
          semantic-token-only Tailwind (no literal grays), required
          <code>data-component</code> attributes, no manual <code>dark:</code> variants in
          components, ADR-tied destructive-action wrapping, and target-naming in confirmation
          modals. Managed baseline for staged migration with stale-entry detection.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each layer runs independently; the baseline pattern lets new code raise the bar without
        requiring full migration of legacy code first.
      </p>

      <h2>Side projects</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">ProfitOfExile</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Open-source Path of Exile lab-farming tool.</p>
          <p>
            Built solo across Go / SvelteKit / Tauri (Rust) / TimescaleDB — backend, web,
            desktop overlay. Web continuously deployed; desktop overlay shipped from cold start
            to usable release in ~2 weeks (v0.1.0 on 2026-03-31 → v0.6.x on 2026-04-13). A
            single Go backend feeds both the web (zero-install SvelteKit) and the Rust/Tauri
            desktop with OCR and in-game overlays — one source of truth, two delivery surfaces.
            Adopted by the broader community after creator coverage.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://profitofexile.top" target="_blank" rel="noopener">profitofexile.top →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">Anthropic Claude Code tracker</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Public reproducible investigation in the official issue tracker.</p>
          <p>
            Isolates a compact-vs-clear instruction-override asymmetry in SessionStart hook
            behavior — minimal reproduction, mechanism analysis, suggested fix.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/6354#issuecomment-3849990217" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue thread →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">Open-source contributions</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Recurring contributor to community tooling.</p>
          <p>
            <code>veiset/poe-vendor-string</code> (Path of Exile community tool) — recurring
            contributor across map mod filtering (prefix/suffix grouping), trade-search
            integration (map yield, quality, 8-mod filter, corrupted include/exclude, instant
            buyout default), and bug fixes.
          </p>
          <p>
            <code>obra/superpowers</code> — proposed smart question batching with empirical
            <code>AskUserQuestion</code> reduction.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://github.com/SebRogala" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/SebRogala →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer class="page-footer">
      <a href="/">← back home</a>
      <span class="sep">·</span>
      <a href="/about">about →</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .frame {
    max-width: 1140px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 32px;
  }

  /* Topnav lives in src/components/TopNav.astro. */
  /* `.sep` is also used in the page footer below — keep as page-level rule. */
  .sep {
    color: var(--rule-2);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 44px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .content {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 32px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .content h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 22px;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 36px 0 16px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .content h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .content p {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .content strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .content em {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .content code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(125, 179, 108, 0.4);
  }

  .project-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .project-list > li {
    padding: 22px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .project-list > li:first-child {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 8px;
  }
  .project-list > li:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 8px;
  }
  /* When the enforcement section uses .project-list, its items are
     short bulleted entries — restore list markers and tighten spacing. */
  #how-quality-gets-enforced + p + .project-list {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  #how-quality-gets-enforced + p + .project-list > li {
    border-top: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .project-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .project-position {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .project-affordances {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    margin-top: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .project-affordances a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .project-affordances a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .audit-figure {
    margin: 16px 0 24px;
  }
  .audit-figure a {
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .audit-figure a:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .audit-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .audit-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .page-footer {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .page-footer a {
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .page-footer a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .frame {
      padding: 36px 22px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 32px;
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .content h2 {
      font-size: 19px;
    }
    .content {
      font-size: 14.5px;
    }
    .project-title {
      font-size: 18px;
    }
  }
</style>
